=== BDR per-sub-block in-kernel (warp-cooperative, PRODUCTION layout) — B200 ===
Device fns: bdrFwhtSubblockWarp + bdrSubblockMinMax + bdrPackInt4Vec + dequantCopyKVarN (mlaKernels.cu)
Layout: per-token 4 sub-blocks INT4 + per-sub-block {scale,zp} f16; rec=272 B/tok (ckv only)
cap: 0.5312 B/elem = 3.76x vs fp16, 1.88x vs fp8 (per-sub-block scale costs vs 3.89x per-token)
Threading = DSV3 gen kernel: 64 vecs/token over 64 lanes (2 warps); 1 sub-block(128ch)=16 lanes intra-warp
Per-sub-block scale is REQUIRED for 128K accuracy (see bdr_longctx_4k_128k.log: per-token collapses 0.866)

